  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Abdul Samad (1St Accused) vs State Of Kerala on 30 October, 2018 Author: P.Ubaid Bench: P.Ubaid In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice P.Ubaid Tuesday, The 30Th Day Of October 2018 / 8Th Karthika, 1940 Crl.Rev.Pet.No.3980 of 2007 Against The Judgment In Cra 838/2004 of Addl.District & Sessions Court (Adhoc)-Ii, Kozhikode Dated 08-10-2007 Against The Judgment In Cc 469/2003 of J.M.F.C.-I, Thamarassery Dated 22-11-2004 Revision Petitioner/Appellants/Accused : 1 Abdul Samad (1St Accused) S/O. Moideen Kutty, Thunnamarakkath, Koyilandy. 2 Ummer (2Nd Accused) S/O. Assainar Haji, Charummel House, Kidanhiyil, Purakkad. By Advs. Sri.M.Asokan Sri.Devaprasanth.P.J. Respondent/Respondent/Complainant : State Of Kerala, Rep. By Food Inspector, Kunnamangalam Circle, Represented By Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala. Abdul Samad (1St Accused) vs State Of Kerala on 30 October, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/31303263/ 1 By Sri.C.M.Kammappu (Sr.Public Prosecutor) Other Present: This Criminal Revision Petition Having Been Finally Heard On 30.10.2018, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: Crl.Rev.Pet.No. 3980 of 2007 2 Order The revision petitioners herein are the two accused in C.C.No.469 of 2003 of the Judicial First Class Magistrate's Court-I, Thamarassery. 2. They challenge the conviction and sentence against them und",
    "facts": "Other Present: This Criminal Revision Petition Having Been Finally Heard On 30.10.2018, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: Crl.Rev.Pet.No. 3980 of 2007 2 Order The revision petitioners herein are the two accused in C.C.No.469 of 2003 of the Judicial First Class Magistrate's Court-I, Thamarassery. 2. They challenge the conviction and sentence against them und er Section 16(i)a(i) read with Section 9(ii) and Section 2(ix) (k) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, and Rule 32(f) and (i) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules. The said prosecution was initiated by the the Food Inspector of the Kunnamangalam Cirlce. The Food Inspector purchased three packets of sweet bread from the first accused at about 12 noon on 29.05.2003, and the bread packets were sent for analysis at the laboratory. On analysis at the laboratory, the public analyst did not find any adulteration, but he found that the label of the sweet bread does not contain the details as required under Rule 32(f) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules. Finding such a misbranding as defined under Section 2(ix)(k) of the PFA Act the public analyst prepared a report of analysis, and sent it to the Local Health Authority. On getting the report of analysis, the Local Health Authority forwarded it to the Food Inspector for prosecution purposes. Accordingly, complaint was filed in the court below as C.C.No.469/2003. 3. The two accused appeared before the learned Magistrate, and pleaded not guilty, when the substance of the accusation was read over and explained to them. The prosecution examined four witnesses in the trial court, and Exts.P1 to P22 documents were marked. The accused did not adduce any evidence in defence. They projected a defence that the alleged misbranding stands not properly and factually proved in this case. 5. Aggrieved by the judgment of conviction dated 22.11.2004, the accused approached the Court of Session, Kozhikode with Crl.Appeal No.838 of 2004. In appeal, the learned Sessions Judge, Abdul Samad (1St Accused) vs State Of Kerala on 30 October, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/31303263/ 2 Adhoc-II, Kozhikode confirmed the conviction and sentence.",
